# Structured question popups (dual-host)

Present workflow options and multiple-choice prompts through a
**structured question tool** — never paste option lists as plain chat
when any tier-1–3 tool is available.

Full protocol: `references/structured-questions-protocol.md` (this
plugin).

## Canonical payload (tiers 1 and 3)

**AskQuestion** and MCP `ask_user_question` share this shape:

```json
{
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "post-brainstorm",
      "prompt": "Brainstorm complete! What would you like to do next?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "plan", "label": "Plan now (Recommended)" },
        { "id": "refine", "label": "Review and refine approach" },
        { "id": "done", "label": "Done for now" }
      ],
      "allow_multiple": false
    }
  ]
}
```

| Field | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `questions` | yes | 1–4 items per invocation |
| `questions[].id` | yes | Stable id for the question |
| `questions[].prompt` | yes | User-facing question text |
| `questions[].options` | yes | At least one `{ id, label }` |
| `questions[].allow_multiple` | no | Default `false`; multi-select |

**Claude `AskUserQuestion` (tier 2) uses a different host schema**
(`question`, `header`, `options[{label,description}]`). Map skill Options
to natural-language instructions — do not pass this JSON blob.

Map skill **Question** / **Options** markdown blocks to the tier 1/3 schema
when calling AskQuestion or MCP.

## Strict priority (tool schema order)

Detect by **tool availability in the current session** — not by
guessing product, model, or host.

| Priority | Tool | Host / source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **AskQuestion** | Cursor host (injected; not all models) |
| 2 | **AskUserQuestion** | Claude Code host (interactive terminal) |
| 3 | **ask_user_question** | MCP `vgv-ask-question` (Wingspan plugin) |
| 4 | Numbered chat list | Last resort only |

### NEVER call MCP when a host tool exists

If **AskQuestion** OR **AskUserQuestion** is in the tool schema, call
that host tool only. **Do not** also call MCP `ask_user_question` —
even as backup, prefetch, or “better UI.” Host tools always win.

MCP is tier 3 **only** when neither host tool is present.

### MCP elicitation ≠ Cursor native picker

When MCP runs, clients that support **MCP form elicitation** may show
a form-style picker. That is **not** the same as Cursor's native
**AskQuestion** UI (host-injected, model-gated). Do not describe MCP
elicitation as “the AskQuestion picker” or tell users they are
equivalent.

On Cursor without AskQuestion, MCP elicitation may help when the MCP
namespace is healthy and elicitation renders. When discovery fails,
elicitation times out, or you are in the Agents window, **skip to tier 4**
instead of waiting on MCP.

## Host-specific setup

### Cursor

- **AskQuestion** is injected by Cursor for some models, modes, and
  surfaces only — check the **current session tool schema**.
- **Composer 2.5** — recommended parent for brainstorm / plan / refine
  handoffs; AskQuestion appears **more often** than on Grok 4.5 or some
  Agent-mode Composer sessions, but is **not guaranteed**.
- **Grok 4.5** — does **not** expose AskQuestion (Cursor-intentional);
  use tier 3 MCP or tier 4 chat.
- **Auto** — router may pick Grok; disable Auto for handoff-heavy work.
- **Subagents / some Agent chats** — host tool may be absent even on
  Composer 2.5; use MCP tier 3 when registered.
- Plugins cannot force the host tool.

### Claude Code

- **Interactive terminal** — **AskUserQuestion** is the host tool
  (tier 2). Use it when present; never call MCP in parallel.
- **Headless `-p` / SDK** — AskUserQuestion is not interactive. Use
  SDK **`canUseTool`** approval flow for structured choices, or tier 3
  MCP `ask_user_question` when the host tool is absent.
- **Clear-context handoffs** from upstream skills (e.g. “Clear context
  and plan”) remain valid on Claude Code when the skill requests them.
  On Cursor, translate to same-chat actions — see
  `vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc`.

## Skills markdown is tool input, not chat output

VGV skills often show:

```markdown
**Question**: "…"
**Options:**
1. Plan now (Recommended)
2. …
```

That block is **input for the structured question tool** — not text
to display in chat. Map each numbered option to `{ id, label }` and
call the highest-priority available tool.

Examples and response shapes:
`references/structured-questions-protocol.md`

## Required behavior

When a skill, rule, or workflow says to present options, confirm a
choice, or ask a clarifying multiple-choice question:

1. Call **AskQuestion** if it is in the tool schema.
2. Else call **AskUserQuestion** if it is in the tool schema.
3. Else call MCP **`ask_user_question`** on server `vgv-ask-question`
   with the tier 1/3 payload **only when** `ask_user_question` appears in
   the schema (not just `mcp_auth`). Prefer elicitation when it renders;
   on `outcome: cancelled`, offer tier 4 or stop.
4. Mark the recommended option in `label` (e.g. `"(Recommended)"`).
5. Do **not** paste the option list as plain chat when any tier 1–3
   tool is available.
6. On **Cursor**, never offer clear-context options — no
   `Clear context and …`, `Start building`, or `Continue with planning`.
   Use `Plan now`, `Build now`, `Continue in this chat`, or
   `Stop here` only.
7. Translate Claude-only context-reset actions on Cursor into
   same-chat actions: `Clear context and plan` → `Plan now`;
   `Clear context and build` → `Build now`.
8. After a **Cursor** handoff selection, invoke the next skill
   immediately in the current chat. Never emit `/clear`, `/new-chat`,
   or copy-paste slash commands.
9. If **no** structured question tool (host or MCP) is in the schema,
   degrade **silently** to a short numbered list.

## Silent degrade rules

When falling back (host → MCP → numbered list), do **not** emit:

- the name of the missing tool
- an explanation that you are falling back
- a recommendation to switch models
- an apology for the format

Mention model choice only if the user asks why the native picker is
missing. Use MCP only when tier 1–2 are absent **and** MCP tools resolve
in the schema; otherwise degrade silently to tier 4.

## Recommended global Cursor User Rule (one sentence)

> When a VGV skill shows Question and Options, call AskQuestion (or MCP
> ask_user_question if AskQuestion is missing) with a questions array —
> never paste numbered options as chat text.

Users can paste this into **Cursor Settings → Rules → User Rules**.

## Handoff options

Post-brainstorm / post-plan / post-build option lists come from the
active skill's SKILL.md. Present them via the priority table above,
then execute the pick per `vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc` (Cursor same-chat)
or the skill's clear-context handoff (Claude Code).
